<p>Thanks for the feedback!</p>
<p>I want to get something out of the way right now, as this issue even popped up in chat a little. This SCP is not a comment on morality, one way or another. It may be anomalous, but it was still built by a human being, and human beings are flawed. Yes, it detects potential and active child predators, but that does not mean its methods are infallible.</p>
<p>As to the last part of your comment, I don't really know how the Foundation could test a person to see why they're showing up yellow, without first figuring out why the thing does what it does. The proper field testing that I hinted at Dr. Darritz starting at the end of the article was initially derailed by Agent Bjerre, so at this point the article is a snapshot of a point where they're just figuring out what it truly does.</p>

							</div>

								
					
